Different Kalman PLL structures can be implemented for carrier synchronization considering either direct states or error states [41], [42]. In this work, we propose a Kalman PLL structure for scintillation mitigation that includes the scintillation phase dynamics in the Kalman filter model with discriminator outputs taken as filter innovations, henceforth called discriminator-based Kalman PLL. We also propose a Kalman PLL structure considering both scintillation phase and amplitude estimation with prompt correlator I/Q outputs as observations, henceforth called correlator-based Kalman PLL. In both structures, the Kalman filters provide direct state estimates since we apply nonlinear models for scintillation. Therefore, as the process models are nonlinear due to the RBF networks, the choice between the two proposed architectures should include considerations regarding the observation equations, where, in the discriminator-based, there is a linearity assumption on the filter innovations, while in the correlator-based, the observation equations must be linearized at each Kalman filter iteration. Other differences regarding both Kalman PLLs are highlighted later in the discussion of the performance evaluation using synthetic scintillation data. Next, we describe the Kalman PLL formulation for both structures using the RBF networks to model scintillation.
